Z||000012||Gokart||03-02-2000||09:22 PM||||It's just below the thermostat housing. About 3 inches long with vaccum lines going to it. Go to <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  and then to exhaust and then to egr. They show a picture of it and you'll be like me "oh, that's what that is"!!||||reg||6
Z||000013||Carrolles||03-03-2000||12:59 PM||||The front side of the EGR solenoid has a large vacuum line that connects to a pipe at the firewall just to the left and below the battery.  Look at the hose where it connects to the steel pipe.  Mine was soft and cracked at this point.||||reg||1
Z||000014||b_b_a_d||03-03-2000||01:09 PM||||Just replaced the solenoid... DOH! <P>Pontiac dealer item.  <BR>Part# 10038324 VALVE ASM 3.670<P>List price $$$  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> $107.00<P>I'm weak when it comes to buying new auto parts!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 03-05-2000).]||||reg||4
